<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>A parallel vector with a given magnitude</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>\(\mathbf{a} = {@cv3(A)@}\). Give a vector that is parallel to \(\mathbf{a}\) and has magnitude \({@M@}\).</p><div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>\(|\mathbf{a}| = \sqrt{({@A[1]@})^2 + ({@A[2]@})^2 + ({@A[3]@})^2} = {@r@}\). A parallel vector is \(k\mathbf{a}\), with magnitude \(|k| \times {@r@}\). For magnitude \({@M@}\), \(|k| = {@t@}\), so the vector is \({@ta1@}\) or \({@tneg@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[validate_numeric(ex) := block([sx], sx: ev(ex, simp), if listofvars(ex) = [] and freeof(%i, sx) then "" else "Type a number in each box, not a letter.");
cv3(v) := matrix([v[1]],[v[2]],[v[3]]);
/* Design: a vector of given length in a given direction, graded by property (either direction scores). (4,-7,4) has a1 # a2 for the swapped test. Source: adapted from SMP AS/A2 Core 4, Chapter 9, Exercise C, Q8. */
alist: [[[1,2,2],3],[[2,-1,2],3],[[6,7,6],2],[[-2,10,11],2],[[1,-4,8],4],[[4,-7,4],4],[[2,6,-9],4],[[6,-6,7],2],[[3,4,12],3],[[-4,1,8],3]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
A: alist[ix][1]; t: alist[ix][2];
r: sqrt(A[1]^2+A[2]^2+A[3]^2); M: t*r;
ta1: cv3(t*A); tneg: cv3(-t*A); ta0: cv3(A); tbig: cv3((t+1)*A);
tswp: cv3([t*A[2], t*A[1], t*A[3]]); toff: ta1+matrix([1],[0],[0]);
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
  <specificfeedback format="html"><text><![CDATA[]]></text></specificfeedback>
  <questionnote format="moodle_auto_format">
    <text>ix={@ix@}, a={@A@}, M={@M@}</text>
  </questionnote>
  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Vectors II: a parallel vector with a given magnitude</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 2.6: Construct a three-dimensional vector parallel to a given vector with a given magnitude, in either direction.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Question 8 in Exercise C of Chapter 9 of Instone, S., Ling, J., Scruton, P., Shilton, S. and West, H., SMP AS/A2 Mathematics: Core 4 for AQA, Cambridge University Press, 2005: graded by property so either direction is accepted, new vectors, randomised over a curated list, with named feedback.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
